      <!-- Название статьи -->
      <h3 class="manuscript-title mb-2">
        <a href="https://github.com/maks-nenashev/Moderator" target="_blank">
          Design and Implementation of a Multi-Model AI-Based Content Moderation System in a Production Environment
        </a>
      </h3>

      <!-- Выходные данные журнала и аффилиация -->
      <div class="journal-meta mb-3">
        <span class="fw-bold text-dark">Wyższa Szkoła Biznesu - National Louis University (WSB-NLU)</span>
        <span class="text-muted">· Research Paper · 2026</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Краткое описание (Abstract) -->
      <p class="manuscript-abstract text-secondary mb-3">
        An empirical study on the production-grade deployment of a fault-tolerant, multi-model AI moderation system powering the FindWay platform. The architecture decouples user interactions from heavy analytical tasks via an asynchronous distributed queue pipeline. It integrates an ensemble of 8 specialized NLP models (v3. v3.1–v6. v6.1), an EfficientNet-B0 computer vision module, and ArcFace biometric embeddings. Governed by a Policy Layer with Weighted Confidence Thresholding, the system prioritizes risk control and false-positive minimization—achieving 94.5% Precision in text and 91.8% in vision under continuous sub-second latency.
      </p>

      <!-- Нижняя панель действий -->
